<header><p class="enc-kicker">Historical factor</p><h1 class="enc-title">Factionalism</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Factionalism refers to the division of a ruling elite into rival groups whose struggles for power paralysed government and often led to civil war. It weakened many states, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk-sultanate">Mamluk Sultanate</a> through rivalries among mamluk households, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a> through noble factions, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikh-empire">Sikh Empire</a> after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ranjit-singh">Ranjit Singh</a>'s death and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ming-empire">Ming Empire</a> through conflict between officials and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eunuch">eunuchs</a>.</p></div>
